<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dynekilen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1716">1716</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dynekilen was fought on 8 July 1716 in a narrow fjord on the Swedish coast near the Norwegian border. A Danish-Norwegian squadron under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-tordenskjold">Peter Tordenskjold</a> attacked the Swedish transport fleet supplying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, capturing or destroying most of it. The loss forced Charles XII to withdraw from Norway.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-dynekilen.jpg" alt="Battle of Dynekilen" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carl Neumann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tordenskjold_i_Dynekilen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The navy was the realm’s main strength: Niels Juel defeated the Swedes at the Battle of Køge Bay in 1677, and Peter Tordenskjold won at <b>Dynekilen</b> in 1716 during the Great Northern War.</blockquote><a href="/empire/denmark-norway">Denmark-Norway · Military</a></li></ul></section>
